  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe rest of today through Saturday...\n\nUpper level ridging will continue to bring warm and mostly dry\nconditions to the region through the week.\n\nWinds will decrease this afternoon behind a cold front and the \nWind Advisory for the Livingston and Nye areas is set to expire at\n2 PM. Additional shortwaves in the flow will move through and \nbring a low chance (10-30%) for precipitation tonight into Monday \nmorning and again Monday night into Tuesday. Late Monday into \nTuesday, the wave is slightly stronger and will bring widespread \nbreezy west winds of 20 to 40 mph Tuesday, with potential for \nstronger winds over the western foothills. Currently, for gusts \nstronger than 50 mph, there is a 20% chance for Livingston, a 30% \nchance for Big Timber, and a 60% chance for Harlowton.\n\nThrough the rest of the week, upper level ridging builds back in,\nkeeping conditions warm and dry. Highs Monday and Tuesday will be\ncooler, generally in the 50s, before warming back into the 60s to\nnear 70 through the end of the week. Archer",
